  </p>
  
  <h2>
    Polymarket Odds Bet Against Cardano Producing Smart Contracts by October 1
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Meanwhile, a polymarket prediction market has been launched that shows participants wagering on whether or not Cardano will release smart contracts by October 1, 2021. At the time of writing, the prediction market betting on Cardano smart contracts has $255,075 in trade volume. Odds show it is currently 58-42 against the project producing functional smart contract technology by that date.
  </p><figure id="attachment_475141" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-475141" style="width: 1280px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" srcset="https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/5842-300x169.jpg 300w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/5842-768x432.jpg 768w, https://static.news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/5842-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/5842.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-475141 size-full" title="Cardano Launches Testnet to Move Closer to Smart Contracts, Polymarket Odds Bet Against Project" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/5842.jpg" alt="Cardano Launches Testnet to Move Closer to Smart Contracts, Polymarket Odds Bet Against Project" width="1280" height="720" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-475141" class="wp-caption-text">The polymarket prediction market odds on July 16, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    Additionally, two days ago, Bitcoin.com News columnist Terence Zimwara reported on Save the Children in Rwanda partnering with the Cardano Foundation. The arrangement became possible after Cardano “installed a payment gateway that allows [cardano] donations to come directly to the project without intermediaries,” the report notes.
  </p>
  
